iterations.reply:
I implemented the node with only `response-channel`. I left out both operations requests because the `with` clause grants no filesystem or HTTP interface. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would each need authority this node doesn't hold. If you want them, the graph needs to grant a log-sink capability and an `http-client` scoped to that host.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // The host channel stamps the session identity and delivery status;
        // pass its confirmation through unchanged.
        aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

